---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import CodeBlock from '../components/CodeBlock.astro';
import Screenshot from '../components/Screenshot.astro';
import { SITE, withBase } from '../data/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Guide — Using Study Agent"
  description="How to chat, ground answers in the active note, use thinking mode, switch skills, and copy replies in Study Agent."
  path="guide/"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="page-head">
      <h1>Guide</h1>
      <p>
        Daily workflows: chatting, grounding answers in your notes, switching study
        modes, and getting more from every reply.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Chat basics</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Open the sidebar with the bot ribbon icon or the <code>Open local study AI</code> command.</li>
        <li>Check the <code>Provider · model</code> line under the input — it shows exactly what your next message will use.</li>
        <li>Type and press <strong>Enter</strong> to send; <strong>Shift+Enter</strong> adds a new line.</li>
        <li>While the model works, the input disables and a pulsing <code>Thinking…</code> shows until the first token. The reply then streams in, and Send becomes <strong>Stop</strong>.</li>
        <li>If streaming is blocked (usually CORS on custom servers), the plugin automatically falls back to a non-streaming request.</li>
        <li>Conversation history is kept in memory until the sidebar reopens or the plugin unloads.</li>
      </ul>
      <Screenshot
        src="images/screenshot-1.jpg"
        alt="Study Agent sidebar with a streaming Markdown reply"
        caption="Streaming replies render Markdown live as tokens arrive."
      />

      <h2>Ground answers in the open note</h2>
      <p>
        Turn on <strong>Use Active File as Context</strong> (the switch under the input) and keep
        a Markdown note open. Its beginning — up to <strong>20,000 characters</strong> — is attached
        to every request, and the assistant treats it as the primary source when answering
        questions about that note.
      </p>
      <CodeBlock title="Example prompt" lang="text" code={"Summarize this lecture note into 5 bullet points and turn point 3 into a quiz question."} />

      <h2>Letting models think</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Enable thinking</strong> (Ollama only) lets thinking models reason before
        answering: slower, but often better for hard problems. The switch is hidden for
        other providers and stays in sync with the settings tab.
      </p>

      <h2>Switch modes with Skills</h2>
      <p>
        Pick a mode with the <strong>Skill</strong> dropdown:
      </p>
      <div class="table-wrap">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Skill</th><th>Best for</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td>Study help</td><td>General questions, explanations, and how-to help while studying.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Revision</td><td>Quizzing yourself, active recall, and exam-style review.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Summarize</td><td>Condensing long notes into key points.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>None</td><td>No skill focus — the plain study-assistant prompt.</td></tr>
            <tr><td>Custom skills</td><td>Your own modes, created in settings. See the <a href={SITE.guideSkills} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Skills guide</a>.</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        The selected skill applies to every message until you change it or select
        <em>None</em>, and it resets when the sidebar reopens.
      </p>

      <h2>Add your own instructions</h2>
      <p>
        In <strong>Settings → Community plugins → Study Agent</strong>, type into
        <strong>Custom instructions</strong>. The text is appended to every request after the
        built-in study-assistant prompt, so preferences like “always answer in bullets” or
        “explain like I'm 15” apply everywhere. Note: it is sent to your AI provider with
        your messages.
      </p>

      <h2>Copy replies</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Hover any reply to reveal the copy icon.</li>
        <li>Click it to copy the reply's raw Markdown — the partial text while streaming.</li>
        <li>Select part of a reply first to copy just that selection.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How the agent works</h2>
      <p>
        Every message is answered under an always-on study-assistant prompt, plus the
        selected skill, your custom instructions, and the open note when context is on.
        The request goes to your chosen provider and streams back token by token.
        Full walkthrough: <a href={SITE.guideHowItWorks} target="_blank" rel="noopener">How the agent works</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href={withBase('providers/')}>Compare providers →</a>
        <a href={withBase('troubleshooting/')}>Troubleshooting →</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
